  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider the vernier callipers shown below. The instrument has no zero error. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math>, then what is the length (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mm</mi></math>) of the rod shown in the figure? [Given;&nbsp;the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>th</mi></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math>&nbsp;coincides with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math>]</p>\r\r<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/633433.JPG\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 136px;\" /></p>\r",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4.5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mtext>&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mi>mm</mi></math><br /><br />Were <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>value</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>mm</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.5</mo><mtext>&#8201;&#8201;</mtext><mi>mm</mi></math>",
